ory" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/state.json" "file_sha256" "7becc90cb0fd23a99b2458b71a48b4031cc64b5450cfe699b8717248b42ac003" "basis" 635 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "There is no $x$-intercept"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/state.json" "file_sha256" "7becc90cb0fd23a99b2458b71a48b4031cc64b5450cfe699b8717248b42ac003" "basis" 635 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the points where the ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}=1$ intercepts the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/state.json" "file_sha256" "7becc90cb0fd23a99b2458b71a48b4031cc64b5450cfe699b8717248b42ac003" "basis" 635 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4}{9} & =1 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2}+16 & =36 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2} & =20 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =\\frac{20}{9} \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{20}{9}} \\\\ x & =3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(3-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)$ and $(3+\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/state.json" "file_sha256" "7becc90cb0fd23a99b2458b71a48b4031cc64b5450cfe699b8717248b42ac003" "basis" 635 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0bf8dc005ff807fc386e7a92f1d75a0fa0012b80de133fc69e1f49058d9876b" "basis" 635 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/state.json" "file_sha256" "7becc90cb0fd23a99b2458b71a48b4031cc64b5450cfe699b8717248b42ac003" "basis" 635 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/state.json" "file_sha256" "7becc90cb0fd23a99b2458b71a48b4031cc64b5450cfe699b8717248b42ac003" "basis" 635 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958862/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-16642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3},0)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/